---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const team = [
  { href: '/about/ben/', name: 'Ben', role: 'Co-Owner, heights specialist, perfect line cutter, great at following instructions', photo: '/images/ben_painting_high.jpg' },
  { href: '/about/david/', name: 'David', role: 'Co-Owner, masking expert, roller extraordinaire, extremely fast at navigating crawlspaces', photo: '/images/david_spraying_high.jpg' },
  { href: '/about/kirk/', name: 'Kirk', role: 'Co-Owner, tiling pro, master scraper, sturdiest ladder ballast', photo: '/images/owners_on_ladders.jpg' },
];
---
<Base title="About">
  <section class="about">
    <p class="eyebrow">Who We Are</p>
    <h1>About Weibel Painting</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Weibel Painting is a father-and-sons business. David taught Kirk and Ben the trade on their
        childhood family home, handing them scrapers about as soon as they could walk. In 2015 the
        three of us made it official, and we've been working on homes across the Eastside ever
        since. Every job is still done by us.
      </p>
      <p>
        Painting is our trade, and we take it seriously: interior and exterior repaints, cabinet
        refinishing, deck and fence staining, and the careful prep work that makes a finish last.
      </p>
      <p>
        Whatever the size of the job, you can expect straight answers from the estimate through
        the final walkthrough, a clean site at the end of every day, and work we're proud to put
        our family name on.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>We Love a Challenge</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The projects we enjoy most go beyond a fresh coat: a full siding replacement, a new deck
        built from the ground up, a kitchen remodel taken from demo to the final finish. If you
        have a project that doesn't fit neatly into one trade, we'd love to hear about it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because we're comfortable across trades, one call to us can cover a lot. Our work
        regularly extends into the trades around painting, like drywall, trim and finish
        carpentry, windows and doors, siding, decks, and tile. If it's next to the paint and we can do it well, we'll
        take care of it ourselves. For anything outside what we do, such as electrical and plumbing,
        we'll point you to contractors we trust with no markup.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Meet the Team</h2>
    <ul class="team">
      {team.map(({ href, name, role, photo }) => (
        <li>
          <a class="member" href={href}>
            <img src={photo} alt={`Portrait of ${name}`} loading="lazy" />
            <span class="name">{name}</span>
            <span class="role">{role}</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 56rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brand);
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .prose {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }
  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 3rem 0 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .team {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .member {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 1rem;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 12px;
    transition: box-shadow 0.15s, transform 0.15s;
  }
  .member:hover {
    box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .member img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    background: var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .name {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--brand);
  }
  .role {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
